From 8eae1ed217fc0b5bb461a85a939b2e48c7e9b3e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:25:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] hyundai: gas interceptor remapped-ID dialect (0x700 TX /
 0x701 RX)

Custom pedal firmware on the owner's car moves the comma-pedal IDs +0x500 (GAS_SENSOR 0x701, GAS_COMMAND
presumed 0x700) to avoid 0x200 = EMS20. Support both dialects, exactly one active:
- DBC: GAS_COMMAND_R (1792) / GAS_SENSOR_R (1793), signals identical to 512/513
- detection: 0x701 -> HyundaiFlagsSP.GAS_INTERCEPTOR_REMAPPED_DETECTED (2**12)
- selection: HyundaiGasInterceptorIDSet auto/standard/remapped (auto prefers standard); remapped sets
  HyundaiSafetyFlagsSP.GAS_INTERCEPTOR_REMAPPED (32), the single source of truth for panda + car layer
- safety: TX 0x700 instead of 0x200, strict RX check on 0x701 instead of 0x201, guards follow the active id
- car: carstate/carstate_ext/carcontroller use the active dialect's messages
Still inert unless a pedal is detected AND HyundaiGasInterceptor=1.
