From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:07:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] hyundai: gas interceptor DBC scaling + threshold from
 bench measurement

The pedal DBC carried per-track scaling copied verbatim from toyota/_community.dbc
(B_raw = A_raw + 475), which this car never produces. Bench (2026-10-03, owner's car):
track B = 0.49413*A + 10.45 (342,290 driving pairs); rest A=465 B=241, full A=2616 B=1284.

- GAS_COMMAND  (A): (0.159375,-75.555)  -> (0.11855,-55.126)   raw 465..2616
- GAS_COMMAND2 (B): (0.159375,-151.111) -> (0.239915,-57.632)  raw 240..1303
  for both 512 (standard) and 1792 (remapped). At the 0.15 cap B goes 1188 -> 400.
- HYUNDAI_GAS_INTERCEPTOR_THRESHOLD 500 -> 420 (C and Python): rest average 353 +/-12.
- test pinning the raw mapping at 0/0.05/0.15/0.25/1.0 and the A/B relation, both dialects.
